   357	def _redirect_collection_window() -> Dict[str, Optional[str]]:
   358	    """Point the primary audit anchor at a throwaway tree for the window between
   359	    conftest import and the session fixture body (module docstring, Axis 3).
   360	
   361	    Import-time by design, for the same reason as Axis 2. Three steps whose
   362	    ORDER is the whole point:
   363	
   364	    1. The throwaway tree and its ``atexit`` cleanup come FIRST (pair-rail r2
   365	       P2): ``atexit`` is LIFO and importing ``audit_emit`` (which step 2
   366	       does) registers the spool drain. Registering ``rmtree`` before that
   367	       import makes the drain run first and the ``rmtree`` last — the other
   368	       order let the drain re-create the tree we had just removed, leaking
   369	       one ``ceo-collect-isolation-*`` per process.
   370	    2. The live snapshot is captured BEFORE the anchor moves. An inherited,
   371	       well-formed value wins (pair-rail r1 P1: an xdist worker inherits the
   372	       truth AND a redirected anchor; re-resolving would return the parent's
   373	       collection tree). An inherited value that is NOT well-formed is a
   374	       redirected/stale one: resolve with the anchors removed (r2 P1) — never
   375	       through the anchor that produced it. Nothing inherited: resolve as the
   376	       process sees it (an operator-level ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` IS the live
   377	       location and must be honoured).
   378	    3. Only then the anchors move to the throwaway tree.
   379	
   380	    Returns the previous anchor values — diagnostic only, never restored (a
   381	    restore anywhere inside the process re-opens the escape at shutdown).
